# Build artifacts (regenerated by CI's `npm run build` before publish;
# `prepublishOnly` in ts/package.json also rebuilds for local publishes)
ts/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# DO NOT add ts/src/generated or src/qontinui_schemas/generated here.
#
# They look like build artifacts and are not. Nothing regenerates them during
# a build: publish.yml runs `npm ci && npm run build` with no codegen step,
# and tracked sources throughout ts/src import from ./generated/. They are
# build INPUTS, produced out-of-band by
# qontinui-runner/src-tauri/scripts/generate_types.sh and committed.
#
# They are also the baseline that schema-drift.yml diffs a fresh regeneration
# against. Untracked, that gate silently verifies nothing — which is exactly
# what happened between 34709ada (2026-06-25) and this comment: the whole of
# ts/src/generated was swept out of the index as collateral in an unrelated
# commit, the TypeScript arm of the gate went vacuously green, and the
# ts-v0.9.0 npm publish broke with TS2307 for three weeks before anyone
# noticed.
